Chapter: UnitRealArith

 Arithmetic on a `unit` type wrapping a `Real`.

 A unit is erased at codegen, so `lower-bin-op` has to dispatch on what is
 inside the wrapper. It stripped nothing, so `UnitTy(RealTy)` matched none of
 the floating arms and fell through to `IrAddInt`: `Metre 1.5 + Metre 2.5`
 emitted an INTEGER add of two IEEE-754 bit patterns and returned
 9222246136947933184, which is exactly bits(1.5) + bits(2.5).

 This was wrong on EVERY input, not on a quarter of the operand plane like
 the ordering defect beside it, and it emitted no diagnostic. `CDX9010`
 guards the comparison emitter; arithmetic never reaches it. The companion
 `unit-real-compare` covers the ordering half.

 `Tick` is the control, and it is why the hole survived: `unit Integer` wants
 `IrAddInt` anyway, so it was right by accident. A test written over the
 obvious unit type would have passed against the broken compiler.

 `Span` wraps `Metre`, which already wraps `Real`. Stripping has to recurse
 to reach the `Real`, and three of the four unit-stripping predicates in the
 compiler used to stop after one level. This arm is what holds the recursion.

 Bits, not a rendered decimal: a decimal render cannot show a wrong low
 mantissa, and the integer-add answer differs so wildly that only an exact
 comparison states what happened.

Section: Units

  Metre = unit Real

  Span = unit Metre

  Tick = unit Integer

Section: Ops

  ma : Metre, Metre -> Integer
  ma (a) (b) = real-to-bits (a + b)

  ms : Metre, Metre -> Integer
  ms (a) (b) = real-to-bits (a - b)

  mm : Metre, Metre -> Integer
  mm (a) (b) = real-to-bits (a * b)

  md : Metre, Metre -> Integer
  md (a) (b) = real-to-bits (a / b)

  sa : Span, Span -> Integer
  sa (a) (b) = real-to-bits (a + b)

  sm : Span, Span -> Integer
  sm (a) (b) = real-to-bits (a * b)

  ta : Tick, Tick -> Integer
  ta (a) (b) = a + b

  ts : Tick, Tick -> Integer
  ts (a) (b) = a - b

Section: Report

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("add " & show (ma (Metre 1.5) (Metre 2.5)))
    print-line-uni ("addneg " & show (ma (Metre (0.0 - 2.9)) (Metre (0.0 - 1.5))))
    print-line-uni ("sub " & show (ms (Metre 1.5) (Metre 2.5)))
    print-line-uni ("subneg " & show (ms (Metre (0.0 - 2.9)) (Metre (0.0 - 1.5))))
    print-line-uni ("mul " & show (mm (Metre 2.5) (Metre 2.0)))
    print-line-uni ("mulneg " & show (mm (Metre (0.0 - 2.5)) (Metre 2.0)))
    print-line-uni ("div " & show (md (Metre 5.0) (Metre 2.0)))
    print-line-uni ("divneg " & show (md (Metre (0.0 - 5.0)) (Metre 2.0)))
    print-line-uni ("nestadd " & show (sa (Span (Metre 1.5)) (Span (Metre 2.5))))
    print-line-uni ("nestmul " & show (sm (Span (Metre 2.5)) (Span (Metre 2.0))))
    print-line-uni ("tadd " & show (ta (Tick 7) (Tick 5)))
    print-line-uni ("tsub " & show (ts (Tick 7) (Tick 5)))
  end
